Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: relaxng.c
Line: 8199
Function: xmlRelaxNGValidatePushCData
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: The function ignores the provided length parameter and treats 'data' as a NUL-terminated string. It iterates with 'while (*data != 0)' (lines 8199-8203), which will read past the end of the buffer if the caller supplies a non-NUL-terminated buffer with a valid 'len' (common for chunked character data). This can cause an out-of-bounds read while scanning for a non-blank character.

